From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Complete coupled center-of-mass consistency contracts

PATCH BASE: f7fdd6eac0cbdbd498e2485c1ccc16b5ac885a40
SUPERSEDES: doc/review/degree_one_com_constraint_followup_f7.patch

Apply with:

  git apply --3way doc/review/degree_one_com_constraint_followup_f7_v2.patch

This version contains no abbreviated hunks. It intentionally leaves the old
compute_reference_planet_mass() helper present but unused; remove that helper in
a later cleanup commit after the functional change has built and passed the
focused tests.

The functional contracts are:

1. g(R)R^2/G continues to normalize the existing self-gravity Green kernels.
2. An explicit positive total mass normalizes only D-Mc=0.
3. Potential, dipole, inertia, and displaced internal interfaces use the same
   committed/current displacement time layer in every potential iteration.
4. Convergence requires potential change, COM coefficient change, and the
   normalized D-Mc residual.
5. Fixed-inner models are not forced to remove an angular-momentum nullspace.
6. Post-solve translation projectors remain incompatible with native COM.

